            <ArticleTitle>Rhodium(III)-Catalyzed Ortho Halogenations of N-Acylsulfoximines and Synthetic Applications toward Functionalized Sulfoximine Derivatives.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>726-729</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.7b00043</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Rhodium(III)-catalyzed ortho brominations and iodinations of N-acylsulfoximines by C-H bond activations have been developed. Subsequent product functionalizations involving cross-coupling reactions provide alkynylated sulfoximine derivatives and benzothiazines with wide potential for further synthetic applications.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
